{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"A drawing whose distances match the graph’s, by stress majorization.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stressMajorizationLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"initial","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},{"text":">? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeLength","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = { _ in 1 }, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-4, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1000) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The target distance d_ij of two vertices is their shortest-path distance with ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(hops by default); between components it is 1 + L̄·√n, L̄ the mean edge length. The drawing minimizes the stress Σ_{i<j} d_ij⁻² (‖x_i − x_j‖ − d_ij)²,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which with these weights is Kamada and Kawai’s energy. Each step updates every vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order to the minimizer of a majorant of the stress in that vertex (Gansner,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Koren and North’s localized update), so the stress never increases. The run stops one step","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after a step that lowered the stress by at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" times its value (each step","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measures its starting stress on the way), or after ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" steps. A tolerance","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"below the default 10⁻⁴ can carry the run past a plateau to a lower stress.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The start is "},{"code":"initial","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or by default "},{"code":"circularLayout(radius: L̄)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Scaled by the mean edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length, the default start makes scaling every length by a power of 2 scale every step’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drawing by exactly that factor, and by any other factor up to rounding. The layout uses no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"randomness. A directed graph is drawn through "},{"code":"undirectedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Gansner, Koren and North, “Graph drawing by stress majorization”, Graph Drawing (GD","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"2004), LNCS 3383, 2005.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Kamada and Kawai, “An algorithm for drawing general undirected graphs”, Information"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Processing Letters 31(1), 1989."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n·(n + m)) for the distances by breadth-first search (O(n·m log n) by Dijkstra when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lengths differ), then O(n²) per step. The reciprocal target distances are kept in single"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"precision for the pairs i < j only, 2n² bytes (200 MB at 10⁴ vertices). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stress"},{"type":"text","text":" and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drawing are those of distances rounded to about 7 significant digits."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every edge length is positive and finite; ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance ≥ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations ≥ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; every vertex of the graph is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"initial","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", at a finite position,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when it is given.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"GraphDrawing","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stressMajorizationLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"initial","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeLength","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"tex